From: Muthukumar <mk@verveflux.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Feb 2026 22:42:52 +0530
Subject: Fix CSS stylesheet DCHECK crash when SheetText called before resource
 fully cached

The original code assumed decoded_sheet_text_ would only be non-null when
the resource status is kCached, enforced by a DCHECK. In practice, SheetText
can be called while the resource is still loading (e.g. during permission
observer setup or early style resolution), causing a DCHECK failure that
crashes debug builds and may produce incorrect results in release.

Replace the DCHECK with a runtime check: if the resource is not yet fully
cached but has raw data available, decode it fresh via DecodedText() rather
than returning the stale cached text. This prevents the crash while still
returning correct stylesheet content at all resource lifecycle stages.

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/loader/resource/css_style_sheet_resource.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/loader/resource/css_style_sheet_resource.cc
index 8d82027d5d2f8d5e6b2daa675fa0b291cfa05eff..c846fb23f0c56fade684ff53f7b9913e56bb840d 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/loader/resource/css_style_sheet_resource.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/loader/resource/css_style_sheet_resource.cc
@@ -136,10 +136,9 @@ const String CSSStyleSheetResource::SheetText(
 
   // Use cached decoded sheet text when available
   if (!decoded_sheet_text_.IsNull()) {
-    // We should have the decoded sheet text cached when the resource is fully
-    // loaded.
-    DCHECK_EQ(GetStatus(), ResourceStatus::kCached);
-
+    if (GetStatus() != ResourceStatus::kCached) {
+      return Data() && !Data()->empty() ? DecodedText() : String();
+    }
     return decoded_sheet_text_;
   }
 
